Nikola Tesla wasn’t searching for spiritual truth.
He was chasing electricity.
But while experimenting with resonance,
he found something he never expected —
a pattern behind everything.

He noticed that thoughts, emotions, storms, machines,
even human intuition —
all behaved like oscillations syncing to a universal rhythm.
A cosmic frequency grid.

Tesla began to suspect the mind wasn’t just a receiver.
It was a transmitter.
And anyone who learned to tune their inner state
could influence reality itself.

He hinted that entire civilizations once used this knowledge,
that energy, consciousness, and matter
were different expressions of the same vibration —
and the secret to all of it
was resonance.

Then his research was locked away.
And Tesla withdrew from the public
as if he uncovered something
the world wasn’t ready for.

